/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  cstr06_jacketed  --  the same esterification as cstr04, now with a COOLING
  JACKET instead of an adiabatic wall.

  The energy balance gains one term, and only one:

      H_out(T) = H_in + UA (T_coolant - T_out)

  There is still NO dH_rxn source: on the elements datum the heat of reaction is
  already inside H.  What the jacket does is remove heat, so the outlet settles
  at 338.8 K -- BELOW the 350 K feed, because the reaction (dH_rxn about
  -2.7 kJ/mol after the acetic-acid correction, docs/design/acetic-acid-latent-heat-closure.md)
  releases far less heat than the 25 W/K jacket takes from a stream 30 K above
  the coolant.  (Before the correction the reaction heated the contents to
  394 K against a 454 K adiabatic limit; that was the wrong exotherm.)

  Check it by hand from the printed KPIs:  Q_kW should equal UA (T_c - T_out),
  and it is NEGATIVE -- heat leaves the reactor (-0.470 kW).  The scan finds
  ONE steady state.  Nothing here is switched on by a flag; it is the same one
  equation in T, with one more term.

  The original teaching point of this case (a jacket pulling a hot, ignited
  reactor down the generation curve, and extinction when it cools too hard)
  needs a genuinely exothermic reaction; a replacement case on such a reaction
  is planned.  No parameter was changed.  The feed pressure (15 bar) is a
  leftover of the old design; the outlet is liquid at 1 atm as well.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        cstr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( reactorOut );
        operation
        {
            V_R          0.005;         // m^3
            thermalMode  heatExchange;  // a cooling jacket
            UA           25;            // W/K   -- overall coefficient x area
            T_coolant    320;           // K
            T_guess      400;           // K
        }
        reactions   ( esterification_etac );
    }
);
